3. Supply all four workflow explanation profiles, document-first interview guidance, and complete phase guidance. It will support small beginner-friendly question batches, vision playback, known/uncertain/blocked reporting, workflow-fit advice, learning/practice choices distinct from owner review, major-artifact review pauses, and bounded/revocable conversational authorization envelopes. Guidance remains digest-bound presentation only and never satisfies or changes a FORGE gate.
4. Supply eleven inspectable, read-only Markdown templates for every listed role except domain-specific `created-work`. The evaluation template must identify exact `created-work` and `acceptance-criteria` revisions and digests, record pass/fail/skip outcomes and limitations, and state that findings do not transition work automatically.
5. Add a canonical project-companion document and workflow-selection documentation distinguishing `project-basic`, `software-basic`, and `research-basic`; link it from the README and relevant onboarding/workflow documentation.
6. Add an owner-observed dogfood guide for beginner game, scientific/evidence, physical-making, creative-writing/song, and clear-software scenarios. It defines records and observation questions only; it contains no fabricated results.
7. Update bundled-pack identities, release/version inventories, installed-distribution expectations, examples/smoke coverage, and tests to recognize all three bundled packs. Preserve exact `software-basic@0.6.0` and `research-basic@0.4.0` bytes, versions, and digests.
8. Preserve historical local Production-v1 candidate manifests and hashes as historical evidence only. Update current-source reporting so changed source is not presented as validated by that old candidate.

## Explicit exclusions

- Core lifecycle, state-machine, schema, authority, transition, or archive changes.
- A new CLI default, new guide/interview commands, template instantiation, automatic artifact registration, persisted batch approval, or automatic owner acceptance.
- Changes to `research-basic` guidance, the direct-agent protocol 1.4.0, framework version `1.0.0`, publication, tag, push, release candidate, or remote CI claim.
- Modification or reopening of existing archives and unrelated cleanup.

## Compatibility and rework

`created-work` is a normal governed output. Revising it uses existing dependency invalidation and requires a fresh rework run with new claim, checks, evidence, verification, and owner acceptance. A changed scope or acceptance criterion uses existing owner-authorized `forge scope amend` returning to `plan`.

Adding a bundled pack changes current source and distribution inventory, but does not change existing locks: source-pack and archived-pack validation must continue to reproduce the existing `software-basic@0.6.0` and `research-basic@0.4.0` identities.

## Durable home and labor split

- **[Sourced]** The durable project home is `C:\Users\kryst\Code\FORGE`, with the governed journal and predecessor archives in its tracked `.forge` state.
